<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wstat (200)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> wstat &lt;unit&gt; [group]
 wstat room [group]
 wstat zone [zone name] [mobiles|objects|rooms|reset|errors|info|path|dil]
 wstat world [zones]
 wstat world dil [ms]
 wstat memory
 wstat account
 wstat creators &lt;name&gt;|all
 wstat count &lt;number&gt;
 wstat &lt;unit1&gt; combat &lt;unit2&gt;
 wstat &lt;unit1&gt; splcombat &lt;unit2&gt; [&lt;spell name&gt;]
</pre>
<p>Where [group] is:
</p>
<pre> (nothing)   : the basic unit data
 data        : the data for the type of unit
 contents    : what the unit contains
 affects     : its affect structures
 descriptor  : a player's connection data
 functions   : its special functions and DIL programs
 spells      : spells learned
 skills      : skills learned
 weapons     : weapons mastered
 ability     : abilities
 extras      : extra descriptions
 quests      : quest information (players only)
 info        : other extras: e-mail, maiden name, guilds, profession, ignore list
 account     : a player's account
 bank        : a player's bank
 ip          : a player's addresses
</pre>
<p>A group can be shortened: wstat fido dat.
</p><p>The others:
</p>
<pre> world             : the game as a whole; world zones lists all zones
 world dil [ms]    : the DIL programs of all zones that have run longer than ms milliseconds (the place to start with a slow game)
 memory            : the server's memory use
 account           : account totals
 creators &lt;name&gt;   : the zones a builder made; creators all lists every zone and its creators
 count &lt;number&gt;    : the first 40 units that hold at least that many units
 combat, splcombat&#160;: how a fight (or a spell) between two units would go
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre> wstat world
 wstat world zones
 wstat world dil 50
 wstat zone
 wstat zone rooms
 wstat fido
 wstat fido dat
 wstat fido func
 wstat room aff
 wstat fido combat janitor
 wstat fido splcombat janitor fireball
</pre>
<p>Wstat displays everything about a unit. All of it at once would be several 
screens per unit, so it is split into groups: the optional [group] chooses 
what you see. It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Set</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Setskill</a>
</pre>




</div>